       </widget>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="20" column="0">
    <widget class="QPushButton" name="resetImportancePushButton">
     <property name="text">
      <string>Reset importance</string>
     </property>
     <property name="toolTip">
      <string>Forgets the per-splat importance the frustum report has been accumulating, so the next report starts a fresh set of viewpoints. Every report press folds its viewpoint into a running record, which is what lets it say how much of the cloud earns nothing from any of the places you have stood - the single-camera figure cannot, since a splat hidden from here may be the front layer from there. Press this before starting a deliberate tour, and after any report taken from a viewpoint you did not mean to include.</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="20" column="1">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="resetImportanceResultLabel">
     <property name="text">
      <string></string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="21" column="0">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="mergeReachLabel">
     <property name="text">
      <string>Merge reach: across / through</string>
     </property>
     <property name="toolTip">
      <string>How far the coplanar merge below reaches around each splat, in centimetres of world space. 'across' is measured along the surface, 'through' at right angles to it - so the reach is a thin disc lying in the surface, not a ball. They are separate because they buy different things: collapsing a stack (through) costs no extra area, while reaching sideways (across) widens the replacement and stops paying almost immediately - on a capture with 5 cm splats, 1 cm across is about break-even and 5 cm loses badly. Start with a small 'across' and a generous 'through'.</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="21" column="1">
    <widget class="QWidget" name="mergeReachWidget" native="true">
     <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="mergeReachHorizontalLayout">
      <property name="leftMargin">
       <number>0</number>
      </property>
      <property name="topMargin">
       <number>0</number>
      </property>
      <property name="rightMargin">
       <number>0</number>
      </property>
      <property name="bottomMargin">
       <number>0</number>
      </property>
      <item>
       <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="mergeAcrossDoubleSpinBox">
        <property name="suffix">
         <string> cm</string>
        </property>
        <property name="decimals">
         <number>1</number>
        </property>
        <property name="minimum">
         <double>0.100000000000000</double>
        </property>
        <property name="maximum">
         <double>100.000000000000000</double>
        </property>
        <property name="singleStep">
         <double>0.500000000000000</double>
        </property>
        <property name="value">
         <double>1.000000000000000</double>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
